#3054
By The Temple Altar~
   You stand before the great altar at the north end of the temple hall.
This is where the fallen wake: one moment dead in the west, the next lying
on the cold stone here, gasping, while the priests of the last breath kneel
over them. Behind the altar a statue of the old god holds out empty hands.
The hall is south; a passage east leads out to the Hospice of the Last
Rites, and the way behind the altar is north.
~
